Stage 3: campaign .CAM decrypt (extender op 0x80) + the campaign-name parser chain.

The CAMPAIGNS mission-select screen (FUN_0000_ec7e) lists 7 campaign names that are stored ENCRYPTED in
armoredfist/FISTDATA/A.CAM..G.CAM.  Each name is produced by: bd14 opens the .CAM, reads it into
STRSEG:0x452c, then calls the extender DECRYPT gate (FUN_0000_e2a5 -> op 0x80), and ef5e parses the
decrypted "DESC:" line into the campaign name buffer.  This patch reconstructs that chain (the extender
op-0x80 decrypt itself is the Doug-Huffman kernel FUN_00007762, wired in the shim fist_extender_gate).

THE DECRYPT (extender kernel, wired in tools/native_main.c fist_extender_gate op 0x80): asm-verified from
re_out/fist_image.bin.  The op-service dispatch table base is 0xcb3 (PM gate FUN_00000f30:
`movzx ebx,bx; mov ebx,[ebx+0xcb3]; call [0xcaf]`, op used directly as a byte offset) -> op 0x80 =
[0xcb3+0x80=0xd33] = 0x7762 = FUN_00007762/776e: a stream cipher over 8-byte blocks, keys 0xfade2bad
(eax) / 0xace4dead (ebp), per-block LFSR update (shl/cdq/and 0xbc9abb09/adc; ror ebp,1; xor+bswap).
Validated: A.CAM decrypts to "DESC:  TRAINING / CAMPMAP: INTR_.MRL / ...".  The buffer is passed in ESI =
(word[DGROUP:0x70]<<4)+0x452c (bd14 0x1bd58), len in ECX = word[DGROUP:0xf810]; e2a5 sets aa10=0x80.

ALL asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (STRSEG=word[DGROUP:0x70]; parse-ptr b899=word[DGROUP:0xf899]
is a STRSEG NEAR-OFFSET Ghidra typed int** -> host-pointer base-loss on every buffer byte; the b941 campaign
name table and b91b keyword table are DGROUP/STRSEG near-offset tables):
 - FUN_1000_bd14 (0x1bd14): open DX = DOS offset 0xf889 ("A.CAM") not a host ptr (patch-077/146 class);
   the read-buffer clear -> STRSEG:0x452c (was host 0x452c = engine code); bytes-read -> DGROUP:0xf810;
   CF (open/read fail vs success) threaded via g_fist_cf so ef5e's `jb` works.
 - FUN_0000_efa8 skip-to-token, FUN_0000_f040 skip-to-EOL, FUN_0000_f05f copy-token->DGROUP:0xf902,
   FUN_0000_f088 match-keyword (token vs the 19 STRSEG keyword strings b91b[i]), FUN_0000_f0b0 seek
   section N, FUN_0000_f0cc copy-value->DGROUP:di: all rebased (source STRSEG, dest DGROUP), CF via
   g_fist_cf (the decompile's local in_CF never reflected the real carry).
 - FUN_0000_ef5e (0xef5e): the 12-file build loop; b941 walk (si=word[DGROUP:0xf941+bx]) rebased; per file
   clear name-slot, bd14 (open+decrypt), seek section 0 ("DESC:"), copy name -> DGROUP:(si+1), si[0]=1.

Proven end-to-end by the shim self-test FIST_CAM_SELFTEST (tools/native_main.c): once the menu is up it
runs FUN_0000_ef5e and dumps the parsed roster -> TRAINING / OVERWATCH / CROSSED SWORDS / AEGIS /
CERTAIN FURY / FIRE HAMMER / BURNING FROST.  The ec7e modal screen + its paint methods (ed28/edc2) +
AE=0 flow are the documented next frontier.

